Original Author Rights
The original author retains full and exclusive commercial rights to the work. The original author may use, license, or monetize the work for commercial purposes without restriction. Any third party (including but not limited to derivative works, modified versions, or subsequent contributors) seeking to use the work for commercial purposes must obtain explicit written authorization from the original author. This requirement applies to all forks, derivatives, and subsequent versions of the work, regardless of who created them.

Form of Commercial Authorization
For the purposes of this license, "explicit written authorization" must be in a documented, verifiable written form. Acceptable forms include signed documents, emails, or text messages from instant messaging applications. Voice calls, verbal agreements, implied consent, or ambiguous expressions do not constitute valid authorization.

Multiple Authors
If the work is created by multiple authors, all authors jointly retain the exclusive commercial rights. No single author may grant commercial authorization without the explicit written consent of all other authors. In the event of copyright transfer, the transferee assumes all rights and obligations of the transferor under this license.

Contributor Rights
